<title>FRANCE: Axa reports higher H1 from Equitable.</title>
<headline>Axa reports higher H1 from Equitable.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurance group Axa said on Wednesday that it expects its U.S. unit Equitable to contribute a first-half profit of 835 million francs, versus 799 million francs last time round.  </p>
<p>Axa financial communications executive Pascal Thebe told a news conference the figure included 570 million francs from operational activities of insurance and financial services and 205 million francs in amortisation of negative goodwill, as well as 60 million in net interest on shares and bonds in Equitable Cos Inc held by Axa.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
